.TH MAKO 1 "27 August 2026" "Mako @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mako \- application server and Lua interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mako
.RI [ server-option ...]
.br
.B mako
.RI [ lua-option ...]
.RI [ script.lua
.RI [ argument ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mako
is an application server with an embedded Lua runtime.
It can load server applications from directories or ZIP archives, or execute
Lua statements and scripts in a Lua-compatible command-line mode.
.PP
The Debian package runs the optional
.B mako-server.service
as the unprivileged
.B mako
system user. During package configuration, Debconf asks whether to enable and
start the service. The default is not to start it. Run
.B dpkg-reconfigure mako
to change the selection later.
.SH SERVER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " configfile"
Load the specified server configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-l [name]:[priority]:app
Load a server application. The optional name and numeric priority precede the
application path and are separated by colons. This option may be specified
more than once.
.TP
.B \-d
Run in daemon mode and detach from the controlling terminal.
.TP
.B \-s
Run in daemon mode without detaching. This form is suitable for a service
manager such as systemd.
.TP
.BI \-u " username"
Change to the specified user after opening the configured listening ports.
This option normally requires Mako to be started with sufficient privileges.
The packaged systemd services instead use the systemd
.B User=
directive and do not start Mako as root.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-?
Display a short usage message and exit.
.SH LUA OPTIONS
Lua mode is selected by a file name ending in
.BR .lua ,
by standard Lua-style options, or by a script following
.BR \-\- .
.TP
.BI \-e " statement"
Execute the Lua statement.
.TP
.BI \-l " module"
Require the Lua module before executing a script or entering interactive mode.
The joined form
.BI \-l module
is also accepted. Unlike the server application option, this form contains no
colon.
.TP
.B \-i
Enter the interactive interpreter after processing other Lua options and any
script.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the embedded Lua version.
.TP
.B \-E
Recognize the Lua option for command-line compatibility and ignore it while
processing the command line.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop processing options. The following argument is treated as the script.
.TP
.B \-
Read the Lua script from standard input.
.PP
Arguments following a script are available through the Lua global
.BR arg .
The script name is stored in
.BR arg[0] .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUA_PATH_@LUA_VERSION_ENV@
Versioned search path for Lua source modules. If neither this variable nor
.B LUA_PATH
is set, the Debian wrapper supplies
.BR /usr/share/mako/modules/@LUA_VERSION@/?.lua
and
.BR /usr/share/mako/modules/@LUA_VERSION@/?/init.lua ,
followed by equivalent paths in the current directory.
.TP
.B LUA_CPATH_@LUA_VERSION_ENV@
Versioned search path for native Lua modules. If neither this variable nor
.B LUA_CPATH
is set, the Debian wrapper supplies
.BR /usr/lib/@DEB_HOST_MULTIARCH@/mako/modules/@LUA_VERSION@/?.so
followed by the current directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/realtimelogic/mako/server.conf
Configuration for the optional generic Mako service.
.TP
.B /usr/share/mako/modules/@LUA_VERSION@/
Package-managed Lua source modules for Mako's embedded Lua ABI.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/@DEB_HOST_MULTIARCH@/mako/modules/@LUA_VERSION@/
Package-managed native modules for Mako's embedded Lua ABI.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/realtimelogic/mako/
Private Mako executable and matching resource archive.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a Lua script and pass two arguments:
.PP
.nf
    mako example.lua first second
.fi
.PP
Execute a Lua statement:
.PP
.nf
    mako -e 'print(_VERSION)'
.fi
.PP
Start a server with a configuration and an application archive:
.PP
.nf
    mako -c server.conf -l::application.zip
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Lua mode exits with status zero after successful execution and with a nonzero
status when loading or executing a statement, module, or script fails.
Server mode returns a nonzero status when initialization or configuration
fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR lua (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mako Server is developed by Real Time Logic LLC.
